# =============================================================================
# VenueRise — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Phase 7A note — for production deploys, every variable in the following
# REQUIRED-IN-PRODUCTION set must be present, or `/api/readiness` returns 503:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   INTERNAL_API_SECRET            (≥ 32 chars; `openssl rand -hex 32`)
#   INNGEST_EVENT_KEY
#   INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY
#   RESEND_API_KEY
#   RESEND_FROM_EMAIL
#   RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN
#   SENTRY_DSN
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN
#
# Run `npm run check:prod-env` against a populated env to verify locally.
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for end-to-end provisioning steps and docs/SECURITY.md
# for the trust-boundary model.
# =============================================================================

# Supabase — public (safe to expose to the browser)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# Supabase — service role. SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Found in: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role key.
# Note (Phase 6A): tenant access now flows through `venue_members` + roles.
# The legacy `venues.owner_user_id` column is still honored as a fallback
# so anything pre-migration-004 keeps working. See lib/auth/tenant-access.ts.
# RLS now honors venue_members as of migration 005 — non-owner members
# (sales_manager / coordinator / viewer) can read tenant rows directly via
# user-scoped queries; write routes are role-gated via requireVenueRole.
# Phase 6C: new authenticated users provision their workspace via
# POST /api/onboarding/create-workspace (no manual Supabase SQL required).
# Phase 6D: owners/admins invite teammates via POST /api/team/invitations.
# Invitation emails use NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL to build the accept link
# (`${APP_URL}/onboarding/accept?token=...`). If Resend is not configured,
# the email body is logged to stdout but the invite row + token are still
# created — share the URL out-of-band.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...

# Anthropic API. SERVER-ONLY.
# Get from: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Anthropic calls are wrapped in a retry helper (Phase 5D): transient 429/5xx
# errors retry up to 3 times with exponential backoff + jitter; each attempt
# is bounded by a 30s AbortController timeout. Terminal failures are captured
# in Sentry and logged as `ai.anthropic.failed`.

# Base URL of this app. Used by /api/widget to call /api/ai/qualify internally.
# In production this should be the canonical https URL (no trailing slash).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# =============================================================================
# Internal HMAC secret — legacy from Phase 1. Still wired in case the job
# queue is rolled back, but no longer the primary trigger path. SERVER-ONLY.
# Generate: `openssl rand -hex 32` (min 32 chars).
# =============================================================================
INTERNAL_API_SECRET=replace-me-with-openssl-rand-hex-32

# =============================================================================
# Inngest — job/workflow runtime (Phase 2)
#
# LOCAL DEV (recommended):
#   1. `npx inngest-cli@latest dev` in a separate terminal — it autodetects
#      http://localhost:3000/api/inngest and runs all event + cron functions
#      locally. NO keys needed.
#   2. Set INNGEST_DEV=1 so the app's queue abstraction routes through Inngest
#      instead of the in-process setImmediate fallback. Optional but recommended
#      if you want to test cron behavior locally.
#
# PRODUCTION:
#   Both INNGEST_EVENT_KEY and INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY must be set or events are
#   silently dropped. Pulled from https://app.inngest.com → your app → Keys.
# =============================================================================
# INNGEST_DEV=1
# INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=
# INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Resend — email delivery (Phase 3)
#
# Used by the scheduled follow-up + tour-reminder jobs to actually send mail.
#
# PRODUCTION:
#   - RESEND_API_KEY is required.
#   - RESEND_FROM_EMAIL must use a DOMAIN you have verified at
#     https://resend.com/domains — otherwise Resend rejects every send.
#     Example: notifications@mail.yourvenue.com
#   - RESEND_REPLY_TO_EMAIL is optional but recommended so leads' replies
#     land in a human-monitored mailbox (e.g. coordinator@yourvenue.com).
#
# DEVELOPMENT:
#   - If RESEND_API_KEY or RESEND_FROM_EMAIL are absent, the app runs in
#     CONSOLE-FALLBACK mode: the generated email is logged to the server
#     console and NOT delivered to anyone. Follow-up rows flip to status
#     'skipped' (not 'sent') so we never falsely claim delivery. Tour
#     reminder flags are NOT flipped — next scan retries once Resend is
#     configured.
# =============================================================================
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=notifications@mail.yourvenue.com
# RESEND_REPLY_TO_EMAIL=coordinator@yourvenue.com

# Resend webhook signing secret (Phase 4B).
# Provision in Resend dashboard:
#   Webhooks → Add Endpoint
#     URL:    https://<your-deploy>/api/resend/webhook
#     Events: email.delivered, email.bounced, email.complained,
#             email.delivery_delayed, email.failed
# Copy the 'Signing Secret' (starts with `whsec_...`) into this var.
# REQUIRED in production. Without it, /api/resend/webhook returns 401 to
# every incoming webhook and /api/health reports resend_webhook: 'missing'.
# RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# =============================================================================
# Upstash Redis — rate limiting (Phase 4A)
#
# Protects the widget, AI routes, and lead-create from abuse.
#
# PRODUCTION:
#   Both vars REQUIRED. Without them, every protected route runs unlimited
#   and `/api/health` returns `upstash: 'missing'` — treat that as a P1 alert.
#
# DEVELOPMENT:
#   Optional. Missing → rate limiting is a no-op (logs ONE warning on first
#   request, then stays silent). `/api/health` returns `upstash: 'disabled'`.
#
# Provision:
#   https://console.upstash.com → Create Redis (Global, eventual consistency
#   is fine for sliding-window counters) → REST URL + REST token.
# =============================================================================
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://xxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...

# =============================================================================
# Sentry — error observability (Phase 5C)
#
# Without SENTRY_DSN the app runs normally and `/api/health` reports
# `sentry: 'missing'`. Capture helpers (captureApiError / captureJobError /
# captureWebhookError / captureAiError) become no-ops.
#
# In production set:
#   SENTRY_DSN              — runtime DSN (server + edge SDK use this)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN  — same value, exposed to the browser bundle
#                             (Sentry never auto-redacts public DSNs — by
#                             design; they're meant to be exposed)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION — surfaces in /api/health and Sentry release tags
#                             (falls back to package.json#version)
#   SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN       — BUILD-TIME ONLY, for source map upload via
#                             the Sentry webpack/turbopack plugin. Not used
#                             at runtime in Phase 5C; kept for future use.
#
# Trace sampling:
#   SENTRY_TRACES               — server (default 0.1)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_TRACES   — client (default 0.01)
#
# Debugging:
#   SENTRY_DEBUG=1 — verbose Sentry SDK output to console
# =============================================================================
# SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@oXXXX.ingest.sentry.io/XXXX
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@oXXXX.ingest.sentry.io/XXXX
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=0.1.0
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_TRACES=0.1
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_TRACES=0.01

# =============================================================================
# Request correlation (Phase 5B) — no env var required.
#
# Clients and proxies MAY send `X-Request-Id` on inbound requests. If present
# and well-formed (max 128 chars, [A-Za-z0-9_-.:]), VenueRise reuses it. If
# missing or invalid, VenueRise generates a UUIDv4. The id is:
#   - attached to every log line in the request scope
#   - propagated into job event payloads (request_id)
#   - returned as `X-Request-Id` on every response
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# Logging (Phase 5A) — pino structured logs
#
# LOG_LEVEL: trace | debug | info | warn | error | fatal | silent
#   Default: 'debug' in development, 'info' in production.
#
# Logs are JSON to stdout. For pretty local logs, pipe:
#   npm run dev | npx pino-pretty
# =============================================================================
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# =============================================================================
# Stripe Billing (Phase 7C)
#
# All three are REQUIRED in production — /api/readiness returns 503 if any
# are missing. In local dev they're optional: the app boots, /api/health
# reports billing.stripe="missing", and any call to /api/billing/* returns
# 503 billing_not_configured.
#
# PROVISION (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the full walk-through):
#   1. Create a Stripe account; switch to Test mode.
#   2. Dashboard → Developers → API Keys:
#        - Copy the "Secret key" (sk_test_…)            → STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
#        - Copy the "Publishable key" (pk_test_…)       → NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#   3. Dashboard → Product Catalog → New product → New recurring price.
#        - Copy the price id (price_…)                  → STRIPE_DEFAULT_PRICE_ID
#   4. AFTER first deploy: Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → Add endpoint:
#        - URL: https://<your-deploy>/api/stripe/webhook
#        - Events: checkout.session.completed,
#                  customer.subscription.{created,updated,deleted},
#                  invoice.payment_{succeeded,failed}
#        - Copy the signing secret (whsec_…)            → STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#
# WARNING: never ship live (sk_live_…) keys to staging. Match the key prefix
# to the environment — readiness logs the mode in checkStripe() debug.
# =============================================================================
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# STRIPE_DEFAULT_PRICE_ID=price_...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...   # publishable; safe to expose. Not used until Phase 7D.
# STRIPE_API_VERSION=                              # optional override; defaults to SDK's compiled-in version
#
# Phase 7F note: Stripe webhook events are persisted to
# `public.billing_events_log` (migration 008) for forensic / audit access.
# No additional env vars required — the audit log is on by default once
# migration 008 has been applied. See docs/BILLING-QA.md §7a.
#
# Phase 7G note: owner/admin operators can inspect the audit log via
# `GET /api/admin/billing-events` (list, payload omitted) and
# `GET /api/admin/billing-events/[id]` (single row, payload included).
# No env required. See docs/BILLING-QA.md §7b.
#
# Phase 7H note: a daily Inngest cron `billing-trial-reminder` (schedule
# `0 14 * * *`) emails venue owners 3 days before their `trial_end`.
# Uses existing INNGEST_* + RESEND_* + Supabase env vars — no additional
# secret required. Idempotency lives on `subscriptions.metadata.reminders_sent`.
# See docs/BILLING-QA.md §7c.
#
# Phase 7I note: owner/admin operators can replay a failed Stripe event via
# `POST /api/admin/billing-events/[id]/replay`. Reuses STRIPE_SECRET_KEY +
# the billing_events_log audit table (migration 008). No new env vars.
# See docs/BILLING-QA.md §7d.
#
# Phase 7J note: migration 009 extends billing_events_log with replay audit
# columns (`replayed_at`, `replayed_by`, `replay_count`) and a SECURITY
# DEFINER RPC `public.record_billing_event_replay(uuid, uuid)`. No env vars.
# See docs/BILLING-QA.md §7d "Replay attribution" and docs/SECURITY.md §10f.
#
# Phase 7K note: a daily Inngest cron `billing-dunning` (schedule `0 16 * * *`)
# emails the venue owner when their subscription is `past_due`. Stops after 3
# attempts per current_period_end; respects a 48h spacing window between
# attempts. Uses existing INNGEST_*, STRIPE_*, and RESEND_* env vars — no
# additional secret required. Idempotency lives on
# `subscriptions.metadata.dunning_sent`. See docs/BILLING-QA.md §7e.
#
# Phase 7L note: migration 010 adds the atomic JSONB array append RPC
# `public.append_subscription_metadata_array(uuid, text, jsonb)`. Both
# billing crons (trial reminder, dunning) now write metadata through this
# RPC instead of a read-modify-write. Closes the race with the Stripe
# webhook subscription sync. Service-role-only; uses the existing
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. See docs/BILLING-QA.md §7g.

# =============================================================================
# Phase 7D — billing subscription gate.
#
# When BILLING_GATE_ENABLED=1, write routes (POST/PATCH/DELETE on leads,
# tours, AI, team invites) return HTTP 402 `subscription_required` unless
# the caller's venue has a `trialing` or `active` subscription row.
#
# Default is DISABLED so a staged rollout can ship the dashboard banner +
# settings/billing page WITHOUT changing API behavior, then flip the gate
# on once Stripe billing is live and trial flows have been validated.
#
# Reads, dashboard loading, /api/billing/checkout, /api/billing/portal,
# team-accept-invite, onboarding-create-workspace, the public widget, and
# Stripe/Resend webhooks are NEVER gated.
#
# Toggle: set the value to exactly the string "1" to enable. Anything else
# (unset, empty, "true", "yes") leaves the gate disabled.
# =============================================================================
# BILLING_GATE_ENABLED=0

# =============================================================================
# Phase 7B — local/CI smoke script env vars (NOT Vercel runtime vars).
# These are read by `scripts/smoke-prod.mjs` and `scripts/load-widget.mjs`
# when you run them from a laptop or CI runner against a deployed app.
# Do NOT set them in Vercel — they have no runtime effect there.
# =============================================================================

# scripts/smoke-prod.mjs — end-to-end smoke. Hits health/readiness, signs in
# the test user via Supabase password grant, drives a widget POST, polls
# Supabase REST for downstream rows, cleans up its own rows on success.
# SMOKE_APP_URL=https://staging.venuerise.com
# SMOKE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co
# SMOKE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
# SMOKE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...
# SMOKE_TEST_USER_EMAIL=smoke-owner@example.com
# SMOKE_TEST_USER_PASSWORD=replace-me
# SMOKE_EXISTING_VENUE_ID=          # optional — skip venue lookup
# SMOKE_SKIP_ONBOARDING=0           # reserved; cookie-auth onboarding is skipped by default
# SMOKE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000            # overall HTTP timeout cap

# scripts/load-widget.mjs — widget POST load smoke. Reports p50/p90/p95/p99/max.
# LOAD_APP_URL=https://staging.venuerise.com
# LOAD_VENUE_ID=<uuid>
# LOAD_CONCURRENCY=10
# LOAD_TOTAL=30
# LOAD_EXPECT_RATE_LIMIT=0          # 1 to tolerate 429s
# LOAD_SUPABASE_URL=                # optional — enables row cleanup
# LOAD_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=   # optional — enables row cleanup

# Phase 7D — when set to "1", the smoke script asserts that a gated write
# route returns HTTP 402 (subscription_required) and that the widget still
# returns 201. Leave at 0 in environments where the gate isn't enforced.
# SMOKE_EXPECT_BILLING_GATE=0

# =============================================================================
# Phase 7E — billing QA scripts.
#
# Two local/CI utilities for verifying the subscription gate. See
# docs/BILLING-QA.md for the full walk-through.
#
# scripts/billing-gate-matrix.mjs — probes representative routes against a
# deployed app and asserts each response matches the gate matrix. Set
# BILLING_MATRIX_EXPECT_GATE=1 in environments where you flipped the gate on.
# BILLING_MATRIX_APP_URL=https://staging.venuerise.com
# BILLING_MATRIX_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co
# BILLING_MATRIX_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
# BILLING_MATRIX_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...
# BILLING_MATRIX_TEST_USER_EMAIL=smoke-owner@example.com
# BILLING_MATRIX_TEST_USER_PASSWORD=replace-me
# BILLING_MATRIX_VENUE_ID=<uuid>
# BILLING_MATRIX_EXPECT_GATE=0
# BILLING_MATRIX_CLEANUP=1

# scripts/seed-subscription-state.mjs — STAGING / LOCAL ONLY.
# Inserts a synthetic subscription row tagged metadata.source='billing_gate_test'
# so the QA loop can move a venue between trialing / active / past_due /
# canceled / incomplete / none without round-tripping through Stripe. Never
# run against production data.
# SEED_SUBSCRIPTION_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co
# SEED_SUBSCRIPTION_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...
# SEED_SUBSCRIPTION_VENUE_ID=<uuid>
# SEED_SUBSCRIPTION_STATUS=trialing
# SEED_SUBSCRIPTION_TRIAL_DAYS=14
